      <section class="estimate-doc-section">
        <h3 class="estimate-doc-h">1. Project</h3>
        <p><strong>Custom roof-replacement cost calculator for the existing site.</strong> An interactive tool that takes square footage, roof pitch, material, and a flat-versus-low-slope choice, then shows a live price range with a clear &ldquo;ballpark only&rdquo; note. When a visitor asks for a firm quote, it sends a complete lead to the existing contact form.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="estimate-doc-section">
        <h3 class="estimate-doc-h">2. Scope of work</h3>
        <ol class="estimate-doc-scope">
          <li><strong>Calculator logic.</strong> Pricing tiers for three-tab asphalt, architectural shingles, metal, and TPO, plus a pitch multiplier, tear-off versus overlay pricing, and a regional minimum cost that you maintain.</li>
          <li><strong>Screen design.</strong> Custom-coded JavaScript and CSS with no outside code libraries. Built for phones first, accessible to WCAG 2.2 AA, and fully usable by keyboard, with the fonts and colors of your existing site.</li>
          <li><strong>Lead capture.</strong> When a visitor clicks &ldquo;Get a firm quote,&rdquo; their entries pass to the existing contact form as hidden fields, so your email shows the calculator inputs next to the contact details.</li>
          <li><strong>Page and links.</strong> The calculator goes on a new <code>/estimate-tool/</code> page, with a button at the top of the home page and an &ldquo;Estimate your roof&rdquo; link in the main menu.</li>
          <li><strong>Quality checks.</strong> Tested in Chrome, Safari, Firefox, and Edge, and on screens 360, 414, 768, and 1024 pixels wide. Before handoff, I run Google's quality test and record the performance, accessibility, best-practices, and SEO scores.</li>
          <li><strong>Documentation.</strong> A short owner&rsquo;s note with the finished work, explaining how to update the pricing tiers and the regional minimum without touching code.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="estimate-doc-section">
        <h3 class="estimate-doc-h">3. Out of scope</h3>
